This tree is /share, and it is read-only.

It comes from one archive that the worker loads beside kernel.wasm at boot and
hands to the kernel whole; the packer is tools/pack.py and the reader is
src/fs/bundlefs.cpp. Nothing here is fetched file by file, so adding a file
means repacking rather than uploading.

/bin is the other half of that same archive, mounted separately: the programs
and the files that ship beside them are one download and two directories.

The mounts:

    /       memfs    the root, and /tmp with it — gone on reload
    /bin    bundle   the programs, read-only
    /share  bundle   this tree, read-only
    /proc   procfs   the scheduler, the heap and the job table, as text
    /home   opfs     the Origin Private File System, and the only durable one

`df` reports which of those /home really is, how much room there is, and
whether the browser promised to keep it or merely intends to.
